The compile environment lacks `ap_int.h`, so I'll implement the wide-bus type using a plain struct of `double` elements instead of `ap_uint`. This keeps the coalescing structure (wide bus pointer types, helper functions, burst params, partitioning) while compiling without Xilinx headers. Each wide-bus word holds 8 doubles (512/64).

